# tools/cl/cluster_mst_subtrees_witness.rish -- the branches of a cluster skeleton, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/cluster_minimum_spanning_tree.rye grows the skeleton and names its bridge edges;
# image/cluster_tree_centroid.rye reads the balance of pulling a whole cluster OUT (a vertex removal); image/cluster_mst_leaves.rye names the tips
# and the joints. This rung reads the plainest cut of all: pull one bridge and the tree falls into exactly two pieces. edge_split reads the two
# component sizes of a severed bridge, edge_balance the larger of them, edge_separator_balance the smallest larger-piece over every bridge,
# most_balanced_edge the seam that achieves it, is_balanced_edge the test. Exact integers, NO float, NO tolerance.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: an EDGE cut and a VERTEX removal are two different splits of the same tree, and the edge cut is blunter.
# EVERY EDGE CUT YIELDS EXACTLY TWO COMPLEMENTARY PIECES -- over a sprout (a main path 1-2-3-4 with a fifth cluster off joint 2) cutting edge 2-3
# gives {1,2,5} and {3,4}, two pieces, where pulling vertex 2 of degree 3 gives three, so the centroid's largest-piece is only 2 below the edge
# cut's 3; a leaf edge cuts off a singleton, agreeing with cluster_mst_leaves. THE EDGE SEPARATOR AND THE CENTROID VERTEX ARE DIFFERENT BALANCE
# POINTS -- the edge cut can never balance below the larger half, so on a star the separator is n-1 while the centroid is 1; only on a single edge
# do the two meet at 1. A lone cluster has no bridge (NoEdges); a non-bridge pair refuses NotABridge. Determinism. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cl/cluster_mst_subtrees_witness.rish

say "cluster_mst_subtrees: Language EN -- Season G the branches of a cluster skeleton; edge_split reads the two component sizes of a severed bridge, edge_balance the larger, edge_separator_balance the smallest larger-piece over every bridge, most_balanced_edge the seam that achieves it, is_balanced_edge the test; NO float, NO tolerance."
say "cluster_mst_subtrees: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the edge-cut split; cluster_minimum_spanning_tree owns build_mst, the edges, and is_bridge, cluster_tree_centroid owns the vertex-removal balance cross-checked here to prove the divergence, cluster_mst_leaves owns is_leaf cross-checked on the leaf-edge cut. A reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading over a reading."
say "cluster_mst_subtrees: Lens TAME -- the cluster count can never exceed the object ceiling, so the flood over a severed tree visits each cluster once and the separator scan runs one flood per bridge; a lone cluster refuses NoEdges, a non-bridge pair NotABridge, a zero or past-the-count id BadClusterId, a self pair SameCluster; all-or-nothing; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/cluster_mst_subtrees"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/cluster_mst_subtrees.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "cluster_mst_subtrees: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "cluster_mst_subtrees: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "cluster_mst_subtrees: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-cluster-mst-subtrees" else "cluster_mst_subtrees: selftest did not print the GREEN line"
assert selftest.out contains "EVERY EDGE CUT YIELDS EXACTLY TWO COMPLEMENTARY PIECES" else "cluster_mst_subtrees: the two-pieces case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "pulling the VERTEX 2 of degree 3 drops the tree into THREE pieces" else "cluster_mst_subtrees: the vertex-yields-degree-pieces fact did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "THE EDGE SEPARATOR AND THE CENTROID VERTEX ARE DIFFERENT BALANCE POINTS" else "cluster_mst_subtrees: the separator-vs-centroid case did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "only over a SINGLE EDGE do the two meet" else "cluster_mst_subtrees: the single-edge-meets fact did not print"

say "cluster_mst_subtrees: GREEN on metal -- the seam a surface cuts to pull a group apart, the two complementary limbs of a severed bridge that bound every vertex removal, exact integers with NO float and NO tolerance."
